THE CORE WHY
Amounts a tenant reimburses the owner for are assessable rental income and the
ATO rental schedule carries them on a line separate from gross rent. The FY2026
folio summary for OWN10905 shows $44.84 of recovered water usage (Dec $6.80,
Apr $38.04) that the model had nowhere to record, while the $291.02 of water
rates paid was being claimed in full.

But the decisive reason is not the $44.84 — it is that FR5's reconciliation is
WRONG without it. December 2025:

  Money In   rent 4,400.00 + water 6.80 = 4,406.80
  Money Out                                 387.86
  Net                                     4,018.94

The identity amount − fees − other_outgoings computes 4012.14 against a stated
net of 4018.94 and reports a CORRECT statement as broken, by exactly the
reimbursement. Every period with a tenant recovery would have tripped the
reconciliation this track is building. The identity is now
(amount + other_income) − fees − other_outgoings = net_received.

WHY A SEPARATE COLUMN RATHER THAN FOLDING INTO `amount`
Gross rent is cross-checked against the tenancy accrual in
lib/tax/rental-income.ts, which computes weekly_rent x weeks. Folding a water
recovery into `amount` would make that comparison diverge for a legitimate
reason and turn a useful warning into noise. It would also erase the ATO's own
distinction between gross rent and other rental-related income.

other_income_note is free text: the categories agents use are not a closed set,
and the ATO reports them on one combined line regardless.

